      <h1>Build and test a Wasm provider with Rust</h1>
      <p><strong>Supported in {{ release.tag }}, pre-production.</strong> You will write an import-free <code>text.uppercase</code> provider, compile it as a WebAssembly Component, prove its interface with <code>wasm-tools</code>, and run it against the real Wasmtime host through the testkit’s fake broker.</p>
      <p>Broker HTTP, broker-owned storage, and command words are build deltas at the end, not a second tutorial.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
